<div class="ring-size-page">
    <!-- Header Section -->
    <div class="ring-size-header">
        <h1 class="ring-size-main-title">Find Your Ring Size At Home</h1>
        <p class="ring-size-subtitle">Already know your ring size, but your favorite jeweler works with a different ring size scale? Refer to the conversion table below to find your size in any desired scale.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Paper Strip Step-by-Step Guide Section (Matching User Image 1) -->
    <div class="ring-size-guide-wrap">
        <div class="ring-size-script-tag">Using Paper Strip</div>
        <h2 class="ring-size-guide-title">How To Find Your Ring Size At Home?</h2>
        <p class="ring-size-guide-subtext">Jewelry making is an art and Sat Jewels is blessed with gifted craftsmen, who have the expertise to handcraft perfect-fitting rings.</p>

        <div class="ring-size-steps-grid">
            <!-- Step 1 -->
            <div class="ring-step-card">
                <div class="ring-step-img-wrap">
                    <img src="/assets/size_step1.jpg" alt="Step 1: Select Ring Finger" />
                </div>
                <div class="ring-step-num">Step 01</div>
                <h4 class="ring-step-heading">Select Your Finger</h4>
                <p class="ring-step-desc">Choose the specific finger you intend to wear the ring on. Finger sizes can vary slightly between your left and right hand.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Step 2 -->
            <div class="ring-step-card">
                <div class="ring-step-img-wrap">
                    <img src="/assets/craft_rhodium_process.jpg" alt="Step 2: Wrap Paper Strip" />
                </div>
                <div class="ring-step-num">Step 02</div>
                <h4 class="ring-step-heading">Wrap Paper or String</h4>
                <p class="ring-step-desc">Cut a thin strip of paper or string. Wrap it snugly around the base of your finger where the ring will rest.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Step 3 -->
            <div class="ring-step-card">
                <div class="ring-step-img-wrap">
                    <img src="/assets/craft_stone_setting.jpg" alt="Step 3: Mark Overlap Point" />
                </div>
                <div class="ring-step-num">Step 03</div>
                <h4 class="ring-step-heading">Mark the Overlap</h4>
                <p class="ring-step-desc">Use a pen or marker to draw a clear line across both ends of the paper strip right where it overlaps around your finger.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Step 4 -->
            <div class="ring-step-card">
                <div class="ring-step-img-wrap">
                    <img src="/assets/craft_polishing_jewellery.jpg" alt="Step 4: Measure Length" />
                </div>
                <div class="ring-step-num">Step 04</div>
                <h4 class="ring-step-heading">Measure Against Ruler</h4>
                <p class="ring-step-desc">Lay the paper strip flat against a millimeter ruler. Measure the exact distance between your marks to find your circumference in mm.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

